  "decision_relevance": [
    "A single base substitution can cause a large, censored loss of DNA competition despite almost unchanged sequence identity; this supports testing recognition features rather than transferring a regulon from overall similarity.",
    "Removal of E43 barely changes hya affinity but changes discrimination in the authors’ additional experiments. Preserving affinity at one reference site does not establish preserved target range.",
    "The 2025 comparison tests the state during the measurement, not just an oxidation treatment applied earlier. Binding recovery after chamber return cannot be treated as proof of oxidation-independent binding.",
    "Different signals are represented: DNA-recognition competition, protein–DNA affinity, and functional repression threshold. Their numerical ratios cannot be combined into one scale or transferred as a direct ligand-recognition measurement."
  ],
